  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> value for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;because the most stable oxidation state of lanthanide series elements is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p><p>It means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is more stable than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>.</p>"
